<title>UK: CHELTENHAM &amp; GLOUCS UPS MORTGAGE RATE.</title>
<headline>CHELTENHAM &amp; GLOUCS UPS MORTGAGE RATE.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>British building society Cheltenham &amp; Gloucester, a division of the Lloyds TSB Group Plc, said on Thursday it was raising its variable mortgage base rate to 8.45 percent from 8.20 percent.</p>
<p>The new rate is effective from August 11 for new applicants and from September 1 for existing borrowers.</p>
<p>The announcement follows the Bank of England's decision to raise official interest rates by one quarter of a point to 7.00 percent.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
